## Orchestration (multi-agent SDD)

This project uses multi-agent SDD. Any agent with superpowers can handle any phase.
The orchestrating agent runs all phases and dispatches independent agents; a human may assign a
specific agent. Humans take part only in the initial question, escalation, and PR review/merge
(never merge). Escalate only under Escalation conditions in the full rules.

### If you are a design agent (brainstorm/spec/plan/tasks)

1. Use superpowers brainstorming and writing-plans skills.
2. At end of tasks phase, generate `specs/<feature>/handoff.md`.
3. Get APPROVE from an independent spec-reviewer
   (`vendor/ai-sdd-guide/integration/prompts/spec-reviewer-prompt.md`), then freeze with
   `orchestration/tools/sdd-freeze.sh`.
4. Commit, run `orchestration/tools/sdd-board.sh sync`, and hand implementation to a fresh agent
   context that receives only the frozen artifacts and `handoff.md`.

### If you are an implementation agent

1. Read `specs/<feature>/handoff.md` — this is your scope.
2. Implement exactly the tasks in `specs/<feature>/tasks.md`. No more, no less.
3. Do NOT modify: `specs/` (except checking boxes in `tasks.md`), `orchestration/`.
4. When done: commit and run `orchestration/tools/sdd-board.sh sync`.
5. Report back to the orchestrating agent, which continues to verify.
6. If blocked: stop and report the reason to the orchestrating agent.

### If you are a verify agent

Pass the contents of `vendor/ai-sdd-guide/integration/prompts/sdd-reviewer-prompt.md`
to your subagent mechanism, then report results, commit, run `orchestration/tools/sdd-board.sh sync`,
push, and create the PR with the `## AI の判断` decision log (`vendor/ai-sdd-guide/templates/pr-body.md`).

Full rules: `vendor/ai-sdd-guide/orchestration/rules/orchestration.md`
